@startuml
!include ../themes/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' SPEC: _spec/_plans/turn-45-draw-stop.puml
' purpose: turn 45 is MAX_GAME_TURNS — HP compare, equal HP draws; not an incident
' status: OUTDATED — shipped cap; product = StarChess
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/outcome.ts
'         packages/starchess-core/src/rules/constants.ts
' live spec: _spec/packages/starchess-core/resolve.puml
'   leave mapping that must stay distinct _spec/_plans/forfeit-as-loss.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' The backlog treated "game stopped? Turn 45 draw failed?" as a hang.
' Live: ""scOutcome"" at ""turn >= 45"" compares ""kingLives"". That is the
' engine cap. Inventing a second draw law would conceal it.
title OUTDATED — turn 45 is the HP cap;\ndo not invent a draw rule

component "MAX_GAME_TURNS = 45" as CAP <<app>>
component "scOutcome\nkingLives compare" as OUT <<app>>
component "equal HP → draw" as DRAW <<app>>
component "**a new draw rule**\nwith no failing dump" as FAKE <<error>>

CAP ARROW_MAIN OUT
OUT ARROW_MAIN DRAW : designed terminal
OUT ARROW_ERROR FAKE : if patched from the title

note bottom of OUT
  **Both kings alive at the cap: higher
  HP wins, equal draws.** Dead kings
  still resolve first. This is not a
  hung UI and not a refused claim.
end note

note right of FAKE
  **A dump that shows ""scOutcome""
  mis-firing is a bug against this
  function.** Do not add a house draw
  at forty-five to paper over it.
end note

legend bottom
  **Do not implement this file.**
  ==
  Open ""outcome.ts"". Reproduce only
  with an export blob; do not map a
  failed cap onto forfeit-as-loss.
end legend
@enduml
